+        loading ``alias`` is the same as loading ``target``. Several
+        aliases may point to one template, and adding an alias that
+        exists already points it to the new target. Aliases do not
+        chain: the target is always the name of a real template, and is
+        not looked up as an alias again. If the target does not exist,
+        loading the alias raises :exc:`TemplateNotFound` for the
+        target.
